{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Grilled Chicken (gai yang)",
  "text": "Grilled Chicken (gai yang)\n\nPreparation time:\n\nCooking time:\n\nYield:\n\nIngredients\n\n3 coriander roots (scraped and chopped),\n\npinch of salt,\n\n4 garlic cloves (peeled),\n\n10 white peppercorns,\n\n1 small chicken (about 400g),\n\n3 tbsp fish sauce,\n\nlarge pinch of palm sugar.\n\nFor the sauce\n\n1/2 cup scraped and chopped coriander root,\n\npinch of salt,\n\n1/2 cup garlic cloves (peeled),\n\n1 cup long red chilies (deseeded if desired),\n\n4 cups white vinegar,\n\n3 cups white sugar,\n\n4 cups water,\n\nlarge pinch of salt.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Using a pestle and mortar, pound the coriander roots, salt, garlic, and peppercorns into a fine paste.\n\n2. Cut the chicken in half along the breastbone, flatten out, wash and dry. Work in the paste, fish sauce and sugar, and leave to marinate for a few hours.\n\n3. For the sweet chilli sauce, pound the coriander root, salt, garlic and chilies into a paste.\n\n4. Combine the vinegar, sugar, water, and salt in a pot and bring to the boil.\n\n5. Add the paste and stir to dissolve. Simmer the sauce until reduced by half, skimming as necessary, then set aside to cool.\n\n6. Chargrill the chicken for 15-20 minutes, turning regularly. Serve with a bowl of the sauce.\n\n7. Eat with raw vegetables, especially cucumber.",
